# Keep the Docker build context tiny and the build cache-friendly. The 2 GB+
# build artifacts and generated data must never enter the context.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-11: an unfiltered context here is 1.3 GB, of which about 1.02 GB is
# things the musl build had no use for — `website/node_modules` (597 MB),
# `website/.next` (343 MB) and the generated benchmark fixtures (80 MB). The website has
# since moved to its own repository, but the Node patterns stay: a stray checkout must not
# be able to re-enter the context. Docker uploads
# the whole context to the daemon before it runs a single instruction, and any change
# under those paths busts the cache, so an incomplete ignore file is not cosmetic.
target/
**/target/
.git/

# Nothing in the Rust build reads a Node tree; these keep one out if it appears.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/

# Generated benchmark fixtures — `bench/*/gen*.py` recreates them on demand.
bench/crosslang/data/
bench/stress/data/
**/*.bcf
**/*.bam
**/*.bai
**/*.tbi

# Editor / OS scratch, and machine-local agent settings.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.claude/
